        <headline>High Surf Advisory issued September 24 at 5:13PM HST until September 26 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI</headline>
        <description>...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR EAST FACING SHORES OF MOLOKAI AND MAUI
AND FOR EAST AND SOUTHEAST SHORES OF THE BIG ISLAND...

.Hurricane Nolo is forecast to continue strengthening south of
the Big Island tonight as it tracks northward. It is then forecast
to move westward this weekend, with the center remaining south of
the main Hawaiian Islands. However, a short period south swell
and strong winds generated by Nolo will produce advisory level
surf along exposed east and southeast facing shores.

* WHAT...Large breaking waves of 7 to 10 feet, increasing to 8
to 12 feet for the Big Island on Friday.

* WHERE...East facing shores of Molokai and Maui. East and
southeast facing shores of the Big Island.

* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents
will make swimming dangerous.
</description>
        <instruction>Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't
go out.</instruction>
